.TH SDL_IOFromFile 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IOFromFile \- Use this function to create a new
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure for reading from and/or writing to a named file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_IOStream * SDL_IOFromFile(const char *file, const char *mode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mode
string is treated roughly the same as in a call to the C library\(aqs fopen(), even if SDL doesn\(aqt happen to use fopen() behind the scenes\[char46]
.PP
Available
.BR mode
strings:
.PP

\(bu \(dqr\(dq: Open a file for reading\[char46] The file must exist\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqw\(dq: Create an empty file for writing\[char46] If a file with the same name already exists its content is erased and the file is treated as a new empty file\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqwx\(dq: Create an empty file for writing\[char46] If a file with the same name already exists, the call fails\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqa\(dq: Append to a file\[char46] Writing operations append data at the end of the file\[char46] The file is created if it does not exist\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqr+\(dq: Open a file for update both reading and writing\[char46] The file must exist\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqw+\(dq: Create an empty file for both reading and writing\[char46] If a file with the same name already exists its content is erased and the file is treated as a new empty file\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqw+x\(dq: Create an empty file for both reading and writing\[char46] If a file with the same name already exists, the call fails\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqa+\(dq: Open a file for reading and appending\[char46] All writing operations are performed at the end of the file, protecting the previous content to be overwritten\[char46] You can reposition (fseek, rewind) the internal pointer to anywhere in the file for reading, but writing operations will move it back to the end of file\[char46] The file is created if it does not exist\[char46]
.PP
.BR NOTE :
In order to open a file as a binary file, a \(dqb\(dq character has to be included in the
.BR mode
string\[char46] This additional \(dqb\(dq character can either be appended at the end of the string (thus making the following compound modes: \(dqrb\(dq, \(dqwb\(dq, \(dqab\(dq, \(dqr+b\(dq, \(dqw+b\(dq, \(dqa+b\(dq) or be inserted between the letter and the \(dq+\(dq sign for the mixed modes (\(dqrb+\(dq, \(dqwb+\(dq, \(dqab+\(dq)\[char46] Additional characters may follow the sequence, although they should have no effect\[char46] For example, \(dqt\(dq is sometimes appended to make explicit the file is a text file\[char46]
.PP
This function supports Unicode filenames, but they must be encoded in UTF-8 format, regardless of the underlying operating system\[char46]
.PP
In Android,
.BR SDL_IOFromFile ()
can be used to open content:// URIs\[char46] As a fallback,
.BR SDL_IOFromFile ()
will transparently open a matching filename in the app\(aqs
.BR assets \[char46]
.PP
Closing the
.BR SDL_IOStream
will close SDL\(aqs internal file handle\[char46]
.PP
The following properties may be set at creation time by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_WINDOWS_HANDLE_POINTER :
a pointer, that can be cast to a win32
.BR HANDLE ,
that this
.BR SDL_IOStream
is using to access the filesystem\[char46] If the program isn\(aqt running on Windows, or SDL used some other method to access the filesystem, this property will not be set\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_STDIO_FILE_POINTER :
a pointer, that can be cast to a stdio
.BR "FILE *" ,
that this
.BR SDL_IOStream
is using to access the filesystem\[char46] If SDL used some other method to access the filesystem, this property will not be set\[char46] PLEASE NOTE that if SDL is using a different C runtime than your app, trying to use this pointer will almost certainly result in a crash! This is mostly a problem on Windows; make sure you build SDL and your app with the same compiler and settings to avoid it\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_FILE_DESCRIPTOR_NUMBER :
a file descriptor that this
.BR SDL_IOStream
is using to access the filesystem\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_ANDROID_AASSET_POINTER :
a pointer, that can be cast to an Android NDK
.BR "AAsset *" ,
that this
.BR SDL_IOStream
is using to access the filesystem\[char46] If SDL used some other method to access the filesystem, this property will not be set\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_OPENHARMONY_RAWFILE64_POINTER :
a pointer, that can be cast to an OpenHarmony/HarmonyOS
.BR "RawFile64 *" ,
that this
.BR SDL_IOStream
is using to access the filesystem\[char46] If SDL used some other method to access the filesystem, this property will not be set\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I file
a UTF-8 string representing the filename to open\[char46]
.TP
.I mode
an ASCII string representing the mode to be used for opening the file\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure that is created or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

